      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Size: height only (6-10 ft indoors), no spread, so unknown. Clemson: sticky sap may irritate skin or upset the stomach; NC State tags it a problem for cats, dogs and horses. Grading and symptoms are the agent's. Interval: Missouri Botanical Garden 'water regularly during growing season, avoid overwatering, reduce fall to late winter'; NC State lists good drainage and 'occasionally dry' soil, no rule. Only a vague rule exists, so 8 stays unchanged and unconfirmed; a second source with a dry-down depth would let it be checked. Pot and season: 13 cm pot, bright indirect light, room temperature, growing season. Dry and wet tolerance days: no source gives days, left as before (from_knowledge_verify)."
      },
